-- title:
--   Ratios of modular forms are algebraic over ℂ(jmath̃)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal G$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb R)$ which is arithmetic (instance `Subgroup.IsArithmetic`) and all of whose elements have determinant $1$ (instance `Subgroup.HasDetOne`), and assume that $1$ is a strict period of $\mathcal G$, i.e. $1 \in \mathcal G.\mathrm{strictPeriods}$. Let $k$ be an integer and let $g, h$ be modular forms of weight $k$ for $\mathcal G$ with $h \neq 0$. Work inside the field $\mathbb C((q))$ of Laurent series, into which the period-$1$ $q$-expansions `qExpansion 1` of modular functions on the upper half plane are embedded via power series. Write $\tilde\jmath$ for the element $\tilde E_4^{\,3} / \tilde\Delta$ of $\mathbb C((q))$, formed from the $q$-expansions of the level-one forms `ModularForm.E₄` and `ModularForm.discriminant`, and let $K = \mathbb C(\tilde\jmath)$ be the intermediate field of $\mathbb C((q))$ over $\mathbb C$ generated by $\tilde\jmath$. The conclusion is that there exists a polynomial $B \in K[X]$ with $B \neq 0$, whose `natDegree` is at most the cardinality of the coset space $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z) / (\mathcal G \cap \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z))$ (computed with `Nat.card`), such that $B$ evaluated at the quotient $\tilde g / \tilde h$ of the $q$-expansions of $g$ and $h$ in $\mathbb C((q))$ is zero.
--
--   This is the algebraicity statement underlying the description of the function field of a modular curve: the $q$-expansion of any ratio of two modular forms of equal weight for an arithmetic group with determinant one is algebraic over $\mathbb C(\tilde\jmath)$, of degree bounded by the index of $\mathcal G \cap \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$. It is used in the treatment of the curves $X_0(N)$, where the index bound is identified with the subgroup index and estimated by the Dedekind $\psi$-function, and in the comparison of Laurent-series base change with $q$-expansion ratios.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularForm_exists_polynomial_aeval_qExpansion_div_eq_zero_of_isArithmetic.lean

import Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.NormTrace
import Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.LevelOne.DimensionFormula
import Mathlib.NumberTheory.ModularForms.QExpansion
import Mathlib.RingTheory.LaurentSeries
import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IntermediateField.Adjoin.Defs

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open UpperHalfPlane
open scoped MatrixGroups

theorem ModularForm.exists_polynomial_aeval_qExpansion_div_eq_zero_of_isArithmetic {𝒢 : Subgroup (GL (Fin 2) ℝ)} [𝒢.IsArithmetic] [𝒢.HasDetOne] (h1 : (1 : ℝ) ∈ 𝒢.strictPeriods) {k : ℤ} (g h : ModularForm 𝒢 k) (hh : h ≠ 0) : ∃ B : Polynomial (IntermediateField.adjoin ℂ ({(((qExpansion 1 (ModularForm.E₄ : ℍ → ℂ) : PowerSeries ℂ) : LaurentSeries ℂ) ^ 3 / ((qExpansion 1 (ModularForm.discriminant : ℍ → ℂ) : PowerSeries ℂ) : LaurentSeries ℂ))} : Set (LaurentSeries ℂ))), B ≠ 0 ∧ B.natDegree ≤ Nat.card (𝒮ℒ ⧸ 𝒢.subgroupOf 𝒮ℒ) ∧ Polynomial.aeval (((qExpansion 1 (g : ℍ → ℂ) : PowerSeries ℂ) : LaurentSeries ℂ) / ((qExpansion 1 (h : ℍ → ℂ) : PowerSeries ℂ) : LaurentSeries ℂ)) B = 0 := by sorry
